  "lineage": "Electronic dance style built in Lisbon's Angolan, Cape Verdean and São Toméan suburbs from the late 2000s and codified by the Príncipe Discos roster — DJ Marfox, Nídia, DJ Nigga Fox, Niagara — running kuduro and tarraxinha rhythms at 130-145 BPM through cheap DAW and FruityLoops workflows into hard, dry, clipped percussion loops, distorted stab synths and abrupt structural cuts with little or no sung vocal.",
